    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only executable test class (the others are a base and a helper), and it passed. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented default registration date on owner creation, returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format. The endpoint is `POST /api/owners`, wired via OfficeFloor functions (no Spring controllers), with DTOs generated from `openapi.yml`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both a create-time input and a response field. The `format: date` maps to `LocalDate` in the generated DTO and serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps it by name automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 After mapping the request to an `Owner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the client didn't supply one; a supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the schema script).\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full build is green. The PUT/update flow (`ApplyOwner`) was intentionally left untouched, so an existing owner's registration date is preserved on update.",
